  ["What an app is", "One ABAP class", "CDS views, behavior definitions, a service binding and a generated UI5 project", "A UI5 project and an OData service", "Entries in the designer's tables, built into a UI5 app per screen", "A model on the platform"],
  ["Where the business logic lives", "In ABAP, next to the data, as it does today", "In ABAP, behind CDS and annotations", "Split: JavaScript in the browser, a service in ABAP", "In ABAP classes bound to the designer's views; the screen in the vendor's tables", "On the platform; SAP is reached over connectors"],
  ["Freedom of the UI", "Every UI5 control, any layout", "SAP's floorplans and their extension points", "Every UI5 control", "The components the designer offers", "The platform's widgets; a Fiori look where the vendor offers one"],
