---
<Page
  current="home"
  title="abap2UI5 - why"
  description="abap2UI5 for decision makers: what you can build with it, who runs it, where it is the shorter path to a UI5 app on SAP and where it is not, what it costs and how to start with one real screen."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div>
        <h1>UI5 apps for ABAP,<br>built by <em>the team you already have</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Your ABAP developers build browser apps for the desktop, the tablet and the handheld scanner, in the SAP system you already run. <b>The business logic and the data stay in SAP. You need no JavaScript team, no extra platform and no license fee.</b> Open source since 2023, in production on the desktop and on the warehouse floor.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="composite">
        <img src={`${base}apps/hero-class-and-phone.webp`} alt="One ABAP class in the ABAP development tools, and the app it produces on a handheld: a table of sales orders with status and amount" width="1800" height="820" fetchpriority="high">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Stats />

  <section class="section" id="the-problem-it-answers" aria-labelledby="h-build">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">What you can build</p>
      <h2 id="h-build">Every process in SAP that needs a screen</h2>
      <p class="intro">Whatever runs on paper, in Excel or in SAP GUI today becomes a browser app. Each card opens a running example.</p>
      <div class="cards four">
        {useCases.map(([icon, h, t, cls, alt]) => (
          <div class="card shot">
            <a class="shot-img" href={`https://abap2ui5.github.io/samples-site/sample/${cls}/`}><img src={`${base}apps/${cls}.webp`} alt={alt} loading="lazy"></a>
            <Icon name={icon} /><h3>{h}</h3><p>{t}</p>
            <a class="shot-link" href={`https://abap2ui5.github.io/samples-site/sample/${cls}/`}>See the example app</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h3 class="sub">One app, every device</h3>
      <p class="intro">The same app, opened on a phone, a tablet and a desktop. It runs in the browser on iOS, Android and Windows, on rugged industrial handhelds too, and the layout adapts on its own.</p>
      <div class="devices">
        <figure class="device phone"><div class="screen"><img src={`${base}apps/device-phone.webp`} alt="The sales orders app on a phone: one order per row, region and status folded under it" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><b>Phone and handheld scanner</b><span>Picking, counting, approving at the shelf or on the way.</span></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="device tablet"><div class="screen"><img src={`${base}apps/device-tablet.webp`} alt="The sales orders app on a tablet: the full table" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><b>Tablet</b><span>At the machine or the goods receipt: the full table, touch-sized.</span></figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="device desktop"><div class="screen"><img src={`${base}apps/device-desktop.webp`} alt="The sales orders app on a desktop: the full table with room to spare" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><b>Desktop</b><span>The worklist and the cockpit at the desk, next to the Fiori apps in the launchpad.</span></figcaption></figure>
      </div>
      <p class="more">→ Browse the <a href="https://abap2ui5.github.io/samples-site/">example apps</a> for the screen closest to yours: hundreds of them, each running in the browser. Or read <a href={`${DOCS}get_started/about`}>In a Nutshell</a> for how it works.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="when-to-use-it-and-when-not" aria-labelledby="h-fit">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Compared with the market</p>
      <h2 id="h-fit">Where it is the shorter path, and where it is not</h2>
      <p class="intro">Four ways to get a UI5 app on SAP, next to abap2UI5. No vendor is named, because offers and prices change; each column describes what you would buy.</p>
      <figure class="arch">
        <div class="arch-scroll">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 950 344" width="950" height="344" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc">
            <title id="arch-title">Where the parts of an app are, in three approaches</title>
            <desc id="arch-desc">abap2UI5: the browser talks to your SAP system, which holds app, logic and data. A custom UI5 app adds JavaScript, a deployment and an OData service. A low-code platform adds its server and a connector.</desc>
