  <section class="section" id="what-you-keep" aria-labelledby="h-keep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Enterprise readiness</p>
      <h2 id="h-keep">Enterprise ready: your security, your process, your release cycle</h2>
      <p class="intro">Logon, authorizations and data stay SAP's, and the logic stays in ABAP. No part of an app runs in the browser, so there is no client logic to secure. Every rule that applies to ABAP, from code review to the four-eyes principle on transports, applies to an app unchanged.</p>
      <div class="table">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col" class="us">abap2UI5</th><th scope="col">A low-code builder in your SAP system</th></tr></thead>
