        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="plain two">
        {governance.filter(([, h]) => !FOLDED.includes(h)).map(([icon, h, t]) => <li><Icon name={icon} /><div><b>{h}</b><span>{t}</span></div></li>)}
      </ul>
      <details class="fold">
        <summary>More: request logging and accessibility</summary>
        <ul class="plain two">
          {governance.filter(([, h]) => FOLDED.includes(h)).map(([icon, h, t]) => <li><Icon name={icon} /><div><b>{h}</b><span>{t}</span></div></li>)}
        </ul>
      </details>
      <p class="callout"><b>No shadow IT.</b> Every app is a class under your existing development rules, and no click-together designer bypasses them.</p>
      <p class="more">→ <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/review.md`}>The review pack</a>: everything a review board asks for, each line with the place that proves it. In detail: <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/security`}>Security</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/authorization`}>Authorization</a>, the <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/security.md`}>security model</a>, <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/accessibility.md`}>Accessibility</a> and <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/verified-on.md`}>Verified on</a>.</p>
